Package: star
Type: Package
Title: Self-Thresholding Angular-Radial Models of Extremal Dependence
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Manuele", "Leonelli", email = "manuele.leonelli@ie.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-2562-5192")),
    person("Dani", "Gamerman", role = "aut"))
Description: Fits the self-thresholding angular-radial (STAR) model of
    Leonelli and Gamerman to bivariate data on standard exponential margins:
    the radius given the angle follows a spliced distribution with an
    angle-dependent Gamma body below an estimated power-mean threshold curve
    and an exponential (generalized Pareto with shape zero) tail above it, the
    angular density is a Bernstein polynomial, and the tail scale is the
    structured family in which the coefficient of extremal association is an
    explicit parameter. Inference is by adaptive Metropolis-within-Gibbs, with
    a continuous Beta prior or a three-component prior on the dependence
    parameter that delivers posterior probabilities of the extremal
    dependence classes. Derived quantities include chi(q), the angular
    dependence function and joint survival probabilities. A trivariate
    implementation with the additive-pairwise gauge is provided in
    inst/trivariate. Core likelihood routines are written in C++ through Rcpp.
License: GPL (>= 3)
Encoding: UTF-8
Imports: Rcpp (>= 1.0.0), stats, graphics, grDevices
LinkingTo: Rcpp
NeedsCompilation: yes
